{
 "name": "volmanaged",
 "family": "volatility-managed leverage (inverse trailing variance, Moreira-Muir 2017), two-horizon vol, asymmetric band",
 "hypothesis": "Realised equity volatility is highly predictable at horizons of days to a month while the conditional mean excess return is roughly flat in volatility, so scaling exposure inversely to forecast variance raises the Sharpe ratio (Moreira & Muir 2017) and mechanically holds little exposure through the long high-variance drawdowns of 1973-74, 2000-02 and 2007-09 while running up to 3x in calm bull markets. A two-horizon forecast (fast up, slow down) and an asymmetric no-trade band keep the daily rule's whipsaw and turnover inside budget.",
